{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/matlab-numerical-computing/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-matlab","title":"为何 MATLAB","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/matlab-numerical-computing/foundations/why-matlab","wordCount":1351,"readingTime":6},{"seq":2,"slug":"matrix-first","title":"矩阵优先思维","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/matlab-numerical-computing/foundations/matrix-first","wordCount":1184,"readingTime":5},{"seq":3,"slug":"interactive-workflow","title":"交互式工作流","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/matlab-numerical-computing/foundations/interactive-workflow","wordCount":1255,"readingTime":6}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"基础\">基础</h1><p>很多人对 MATLAB 的第一印象是&quot;贵、封闭、学校里用的&quot;，这些标签都不算错，却都没说到它真正的价值所在。这一章的任务，是把 MATLAB 从一堆刻板印象里拽出来，还原成它本来的样子：一套以矩阵为中心、以交互试错为节奏的数值计算环境。</p>\n<p>三篇文档对应三个递进的问题。<a href=\"why-matlab\">为何 MATLAB</a> 回答&quot;它到底解决谁的问题&quot;——梳理它从 1984 年商业化至今、到 2026 年 R2026a 版本的定位演化，以及在开源替代环伺下它凭什么还活着。<a href=\"matrix-first\">矩阵优先思维</a> 回答&quot;用它写代码时该如何思考&quot;——这是整个 hub 的认知地基，标量即 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1\\times 1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span></span> 矩阵、一切优先想成数组运算、循环是性能反模式。<a href=\"interactive-workflow\">交互式工作流</a> 回答&quot;它为什么让人产出快&quot;——命令行即时反馈、Live Script 把代码与结果织在一起、断点调试随手可得。</p>\n<p>这一章不教任何具体的数值算法，那是后面三章的事。它只负责让你在打开 MATLAB 命令窗口的那一刻，脑子里装的是对的世界观：先把问题想成矩阵，再用交互的方式逼近答案。建立了这个基调，<a href=\"../language/\">语言</a> 章的向量化、函数、数据类型才会顺理成章，而不是一堆需要死记的语法规则。建议三篇按顺序读，尤其矩阵优先思维一篇，是后面所有内容反复回指的锚点。</p>\n"}